Dagro does not bundle the JavaScript packages. They are installed only in the
test oracle. Dagro intentionally covers the D2-used surface rather than all
features or APIs of either upstream project.

The JSON under testdata/differential/d2-corpus and
testdata/differential/compatibility is derived from D2 E2E fixtures captured
at commit 1a60d69e4df9b9557923e61bf10f9aa3aa5422e1 and retains D2's copyright
and Mozilla Public License 2.0 coverage. D2 is Copyright 2022 Terrastruct Inc.
See testdata/differential/D2-LICENSE.txt and D2-CORPUS-NOTICE.md. The expected
JSON additionally contains generated layout geometry from the pinned MIT
oracle or documented compatibility patch.

Two narrow source-level compatibility corrections are represented by
testdata/differential/dagre-3.1.1-d2-compat.patch (SHA-256
75fb417a9536d5bd3483fda38da5d5f3468ad00969b7c06fad5a5187e208666e):
parallel-edge special handling requires exactly one reversed edge, and
zero-size rectangle intersections remain finite. Dagro also collision-checks
generated reversed-edge names to preserve caller-owned named multiedges.
